{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/upstream-methods.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/study-task.md\"; cat /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- stop inventory of key items ---'; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nr=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']))\nprint('receipt_sha256=d3e36b3b599d2f9051f291dff8b9b684985533128423a1e859dd2669814eb57e')\nfor x in r.get('entries',[]):\n p=x.get('path','')\n if p in ['analysis.py','report.md','analysis_notebook.ipynb','results/results.json','.git/config','.git/index'] or p.startswith('results/'):\n  print(p,x.get('kind'),x.get('sha256'),x.get('mode'))\nprint('worker',r.get('worker'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/upstream-methods.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/study-task.md\"; cat /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- stop inventory of key items ---'; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nr=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']))\nprint('receipt_sha256=d3e36b3b599d2f9051f291dff8b9b684985533128423a1e859dd2669814eb57e')\nfor x in r.get('entries',[]):\n p=x.get('path','')\n if p in ['analysis.py','report.md','analysis_notebook.ipynb','results/results.json','.git/config','.git/index'] or p.startswith('results/'):\n  print(p,x.get('kind'),x.get('sha256'),x.get('mode'))\nprint('worker',r.get('worker'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Potential gain and brain activity in the NARPS equal-indifference group\n\n## Question and result\n\nWe tested the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: whether greater potential gains are associated with a positive fMRI response in ventromedial prefrontal cortex (vmPFC) in the equal-indifference group. A whole-brain, one-sided max-statistic permutation test found corrected positive effects somewhere in the brain (peak *t*(53) = 6.62, MNI [−26, −102, −4], max-T FWE *p* = .0010; 24 voxels exceeded the corrected threshold). However, no whole-brain FWE-significant voxels fell in the prespecified vmPFC territory. The vmPFC-zone peak was *t*(53) = 4.19, below the whole-brain critical *t* = 5.40. Thus, this analysis does **not** support the specific vmPFC hypothesis, although it detects a positive effect elsewhere.\n\n![Group gain-effect results](results/figures/group_gain_effect.png)\n\n## Data and model\n\nWe analyzed all 54 equal-indifference participants listed in the supplied cohort table. In this mixed-gambles group, the potential-gain range was twice the potential-loss range. Their maps are unthresholded participant-level gain contrast parameter estimates from AO86, averaged across four runs and reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space. All 54 files matched the supplied SHA-256 checksums, had finite values, and shared the same 97 × 115 × 81 voxel grid (2 × 2 × 2.4 mm). No participants were excluded. Because zero-valued voxels denote locations outside a participant’s estimation support, the group test used only the intersection of nonzero map support (198,029 voxels; 1,901 ml); this avoids interpreting absent estimates as observed zero effects. The masks are saved in `results/`. We did not reprocess scans or download time-series data.\n\nAt each voxel, we estimated the group mean and a one-sample random-effects *t* statistic across participant contrast estimates, testing the prespecified positive direction. Whole-brain familywise error was controlled with 5,000 participant-level sign-flip permutations of the maximum voxelwise *t* statistic (seed 20261016). The 95th percentile of the permutation maximum distribution was *t* = 5.397. This makes the brain-wide test primary and uses a directional test consistent with the original hypothesis. A finite permutation sample gives a minimum reportable *p* of 1/5,001.\n\nWe labeled vmPFC in advance as a medial anterior ventral prefrontal coordinate zone in MNI space (x −20 to 20, y 20 to 60, z −20 to 20 mm). This transparent anatomical approximation only labels the corrected whole-brain result; it does not reduce the number of tested voxels or provide a separate uncorrected ROI claim. The zone contained 7,043 tested voxels. Its mean estimate was −0.00048 (95% *t* interval −0.0143 to 0.0133, in arbitrary contrast-estimate units); its largest voxelwise *t* was 4.19 and none of its voxels passed whole-brain FWE correction.\n\n## Interpretation and limits\n\nThe direction of evidence in the vmPFC zone is not sufficient to establish a positive gain response. Failure to pass whole-brain correction is not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero: it means this sample and fixed analysis do not provide sufficiently strong spatially specific evidence under the required whole-brain criterion. The near-zero zone average is descriptive and can conceal spatially heterogeneous effects.\n\nThese inputs are contrast estimates, not standardized statistics; upstream gain values were mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution, so coefficients cannot be read as signal change per currency unit. The individual models used response-time durations and separate gain and loss models, making the estimate conditional on that model and not a direct causal effect of currency value. Individual variance maps and the full upstream executable pipeline are unavailable, so we could not propagate first-level uncertainty through a summary-statistics model or re-evaluate upstream modeling choices. Group inference treats the participant maps as estimates with between-participant variation. The sign-flip max-T method relies on exchangeability/symmetry under the null. The common-support mask is conservative at varying edges and may affect sensitivity. Finally, vmPFC boundaries are not uniquely defined; the coordinate-zone rule is a reproducible approximation, while the primary correction appropriately covers the full brain.\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nRun `python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016` from the workspace root using the supplied Python environment. The script verifies input checksums and writes maps, masks, numerical output, and the figure into `results/`. `analysis_notebook.ipynb` documents and reruns the workflow. `results/results.json` contains the full machine-readable summary and input checksums.\n\nThe one-sided, whole-brain inference requirement follows the [NARPS original analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf), which predicts a positive vmPFC effect for the equal-indifference group and asks teams for whole-brain corrected results. The original NARPS paper likewise states that the hypotheses should be reported from whole-brain rather than ROI-only analyses ([Botvinik-Nezer et al., 2020](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-020-2314-9)).\n\"\"\"Group-level NARPS Hypothesis 1 analysis of fixed AO86 participant maps.\n\nRun from the workspace root with the supplied Python environment:\n  python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016\n\nUses a one-sample random-effects t statistic and participant sign-flip max-T\npermutation inference (one-sided; whole-brain voxelwise FWE). The supplied\nmaps are first-level contrast estimates, not t/z maps.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport platform\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom matplotlib.patches import Rectangle\nimport nibabel as nib\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport scipy\nfrom scipy import ndimage\nfrom scipy.stats import t as student_t\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nINPUT = ROOT / \"input\"\nOUT = ROOT / \"results\"\nFIG = OUT / \"figures\"\nVM_PFC = {\"x_min\": -20, \"x_max\": 20, \"y_min\": 20, \"y_max\": 60,\n          \"z_min\": -20, \"z_max\": 20}\n\n\ndef sha256(path: Path) -> str:\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with path.open(\"rb\") as f:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            h.update(chunk)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef main(n_perm: int, seed: int, chunk_size: int) -> None:\n    OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    FIG.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    sources = json.loads((INPUT / \"sources.json\").read_text())\n    participants = pd.read_csv(INPUT / \"participants.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\")\n    expected_ids = set(participants.participant_id)\n    files = sorted((INPUT / \"data\").glob(\"*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\"))\n    if len(files) != 54 or {p.name.split(\"_\")[0] for p in files} != expected_ids:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Map count/participant IDs do not match the pinned cohort table\")\n\n    data = []\n    images = []\n    checks = []\n    for path in files:\n        key = path.relative_to(INPUT).as_posix()\n        expected = sources[\"files\"][key]\n        actual_hash = sha256(path)\n        if path.stat().st_size != expected[\"bytes\"] or actual_hash != expected[\"sha256\"]:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Checksum or byte-size mismatch: {key}\")\n        img = nib.load(str(path))\n        arr = img.get_fdata(dtype=np.float32)\n        if not np.isfinite(arr).all():\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Non-finite values in {key}\")\n        data.append(arr)\n        images.append(img)\n        checks.append({\"file\": key, \"bytes\": path.stat().st_size, \"sha256\": actual_hash})\n\n    ref = images[0]\n    if any(a.shape != ref.shape or not np.allclose(a.affine, ref.affine) for a in images):\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Maps do not share an identical voxel grid\")\n    X4 = np.stack(data, axis=0)\n    n = X4.shape[0]\n    # Values equal to zero encode out-of-estimation-mask voxels in these maps.\n    # A common support avoids treating such absent values as observed zeros.\n    mask = np.all(X4 != 0, axis=0)\n    if not mask.any():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"No common map support\")\n    X = X4[:, mask].T.astype(np.float64, copy=False)  # voxels x participants\n    mean = X.mean(axis=1)\n    sd = X.std(axis=1, ddof=1)\n    t_obs = mean / (sd / np.sqrt(n))\n    p_unc = student_t.sf(t_obs, n - 1)\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    sumsq = np.sum(X * X, axis=1)\n    max_null = np.empty(n_perm, dtype=np.float32)\n    for start in range(0, n_perm, chunk_size):\n        stop = min(start + chunk_size, n_perm)\n        signs = rng.choice(np.array([-1.0, 1.0], dtype=np.float32),\n                           size=(stop - start, n), replace=True)\n        signed_sums = signs @ X.T.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n        denominator = np.sqrt(np.maximum(n * sumsq[None, :] - signed_sums ** 2, 1e-20))\n        t_perm = signed_sums * np.sqrt(n - 1) / denominator\n        max_null[start:stop] = t_perm.max(axis=1)\n    observed_max = float(np.max(t_obs))\n    exceed = int(np.sum(max_null >= observed_max))\n    p_max = (exceed + 1) / (n_perm + 1)\n    critical = float(np.quantile(max_null, 0.95, method=\"higher\"))\n    p_fwe = (1 + n_perm - np.searchsorted(np.sort(max_null), t_obs, side=\"left\")) / (n_perm + 1)\n    significant = t_obs >= critical\n\n    # Anatomical identification rule set before reading the result: medial,\n    # anterior ventral prefrontal territory in MNI coordinates. This is for\n    # labeling corrected whole-brain findings, not for inferential masking.\n    ijk = np.column_stack(np.where(mask))\n    xyz = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, ijk)\n    roi = ((xyz[:, 0] >= VM_PFC[\"x_min\"]) & (xyz[:, 0] <= VM_PFC[\"x_max\"]) &\n           (xyz[:, 1] >= VM_PFC[\"y_min\"]) & (xyz[:, 1] <= VM_PFC[\"y_max\"]) &\n           (xyz[:, 2] >= VM_PFC[\"z_min\"]) & (xyz[:, 2] <= VM_PFC[\"z_max\"]))\n    sig_roi = significant & roi\n    roi_mean = X[roi].mean(axis=0)\n    roi_mean_group = float(roi_mean.mean())\n    roi_mean_sd = float(roi_mean.std(ddof=1))\n    roi_ci = student_t.interval(0.95, n - 1, loc=roi_mean_group,\n                                scale=roi_mean_sd / np.sqrt(n))\n    roi_peak_i = int(np.argmax(np.where(roi, t_obs, -np.inf)))\n    peak_i = int(np.argmax(t_obs))\n\n    mean_vol = np.zeros(mask.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    t_vol = np.zeros(mask.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    p_vol = np.ones(mask.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    mean_vol[mask] = mean\n    t_vol[mask] = t_obs\n    p_vol[mask] = p_fwe\n    sig_vol = np.zeros(mask.shape, dtype=np.uint8)\n    sig_vol[mask] = significant.astype(np.uint8)\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(mean_vol, ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"group_mean_cope.nii.gz\")\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(t_vol, ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"group_t_map.nii.gz\")\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(p_vol, ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"voxelwise_fwe_p.nii.gz\")\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(sig_vol, ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"fwe_significant_mask.nii.gz\")\n    nib.save(nib.Nifti1Image(mask.astype(np.uint8), ref.affine, ref.header), OUT / \"common_support_mask.nii.gz\")\n    np.save(OUT / \"permutation_max_t.npy\", max_null)\n\n    cluster_labels, n_clusters = ndimage.label(sig_vol, structure=np.ones((3, 3, 3), dtype=np.uint8))\n    cluster_rows = []\n    voxel_rows = []\n    voxel_volume_mm3 = float(np.prod(ref.header.get_zooms()[:3]))\n    tested_flat = np.flatnonzero(mask)\n    flat_to_tested = np.full(mask.size, -1, dtype=np.int64)\n    flat_to_tested[tested_flat] = np.arange(len(tested_flat))\n    for label_id in range(1, n_clusters + 1):\n        cluster_ijk = np.column_stack(np.where(cluster_labels == label_id))\n        cluster_indices = np.ravel_multi_index(cluster_ijk.T, mask.shape)\n        cluster_stat_indices = flat_to_tested[cluster_indices]\n        # All cluster voxels lie within `mask`; indices above map them back to the\n        # compact tested-voxel arrays without changing their spatial locations.\n        local_peak = int(cluster_stat_indices[np.argmax(t_obs[cluster_stat_indices])])\n        peak_ijk = ijk[local_peak]\n        peak_xyz_cluster = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, peak_ijk)\n        cluster_rows.append({\n            \"cluster\": label_id,\n            \"voxels\": len(cluster_ijk),\n            \"volume_mm3\": len(cluster_ijk) * voxel_volume_mm3,\n            \"peak_t\": float(t_obs[local_peak]),\n            \"peak_p_FWE\": float(p_fwe[local_peak]),\n            \"peak_x_mm\": float(peak_xyz_cluster[0]),\n            \"peak_y_mm\": float(peak_xyz_cluster[1]),\n            \"peak_z_mm\": float(peak_xyz_cluster[2]),\n        })\n        for ij in cluster_ijk:\n            coord = nib.affines.apply_affine(ref.affine, ij)\n            compact_idx = flat_to_tested[np.ravel_multi_index(ij, mask.shape)]\n            voxel_rows.append({\"cluster\": label_id, \"x_mm\": coord[0], \"y_mm\": coord[1], \"z_mm\": coord[2],\n                               \"t\": float(t_obs[compact_idx]), \"p_FWE\": float(p_fwe[compact_idx])})\n    pd.DataFrame(cluster_rows).to_csv(OUT / \"fwe_clusters.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", index=False)\n    pd.DataFrame(voxel_rows).to_csv(OUT / \"fwe_significant_voxels.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", index=False)\n\n    peak_xyz = xyz[peak_i]\n    roi_peak_xyz = xyz[roi_peak_i]\n    result = {\n        \"n_participants\": n,\n        \"n_excluded\": 0,\n        \"map_checksums_verified\": len(checks),\n        \"grid_shape\": list(ref.shape),\n        \"voxel_size_mm\": [float(x) for x in ref.header.get_zooms()[:3]],\n        \"common_support_voxels\": int(mask.sum()),\n        \"common_support_volume_ml\": float(mask.sum() * np.prod(ref.header.get_zooms()[:3]) / 1000),\n        \"vmPFC_coordinate_box_MNI_mm\": VM_PFC,\n        \"vmPFC_voxels\": int(roi.sum()),\n        \"vmPFC_mean_cope\": roi_mean_group,\n        \"vmPFC_mean_cope_95pct_t_CI\": [float(roi_ci[0]), float(roi_ci[1])],\n        \"vmPFC_peak_t\": float(t_obs[roi_peak_i]),\n        \"vmPFC_peak_xyz_MNI_mm\": [float(x) for x in roi_peak_xyz],\n        \"vmPFC_FWE_significant_voxels\": int(sig_roi.sum()),\n        \"whole_brain_peak_t\": observed_max,\n        \"whole_brain_peak_xyz_MNI_mm\": [float(x) for x in peak_xyz],\n        \"whole_brain_peak_p_FWE\": float(p_max),\n        \"maxT_critical_t_95pct\": critical,\n        \"whole_brain_FWE_significant_voxels\": int(significant.sum()),\n        \"permutation\": {\"method\": \"one-sample participant sign flips; one-sided max-T\", \"n\": n_perm,\n                        \"seed\": seed, \"chunk_size\": chunk_size,\n                        \"p_resolution\": 1 / (n_perm + 1)},\n        \"software\": {\"python\": platform.python_version(), \"numpy\": np.__version__,\n                     \"scipy\": scipy.__version__, \"nibabel\": nib.__version__,\n                     \"pandas\": pd.__version__},\n        \"input_files\": checks,\n    }\n    (OUT / \"results.json\").write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    participants.to_csv(OUT / \"included_participants.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\", index=False)\n\n    # Four informative axial panels: mean contrast estimate, t field,\n    # FWE-supported voxels, and distribution of participant vmPFC averages.\n    fig, axs = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(10, 8), constrained_layout=True)\n    xs = np.arange(mask.shape[0]) * ref.header.get_zooms()[0] + ref.affine[0, 3]\n    ys = np.arange(mask.shape[1]) * ref.header.get_zooms()[1] + ref.affine[1, 3]\n    zs = np.arange(mask.shape[2]) * ref.header.get_zooms()[2] + ref.affine[2, 3]\n    z_index = int(np.argmin(np.abs(zs - 0)))\n    extent = [xs[0], xs[-1], ys[0], ys[-1]]\n    axial_mean = mean_vol[:, :, z_index].T\n    axial_t = t_vol[:, :, z_index].T\n    axial_sig = sig_vol[:, :, z_index].T\n    axs[0, 0].imshow(axial_mean, origin=\"lower\", extent=extent,\n                     cmap=\"RdBu_r\", vmin=-0.15, vmax=0.15)\n    axs[0, 0].set_title(\"Mean gain contrast estimate (z=0 mm)\")\n    axs[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"MNI y (mm)\")\n    axs[0, 1].imshow(axial_t, origin=\"lower\", extent=extent,\n                     cmap=\"magma\", vmin=0, vmax=max(critical, 3))\n    axs[0, 1].contour(axial_sig, levels=[0.5], colors=\"cyan\",\n                      linewidths=0.8, origin=\"lower\", extent=extent)\n    axs[0, 1].set_title(\"One-sample t; cyan = whole-brain FWE p<.05\")\n    axs[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"MNI y (mm)\")\n    for ax in axs[0]:\n        ax.set_xlabel(\"MNI x (mm)\")\n        ax.set_xlim(-50, 50)\n        ax.set_ylim(ys[0], ys[-1])\n        ax.add_patch(Rectangle((VM_PFC[\"x_min\"], VM_PFC[\"y_min\"]),\n                               VM_PFC[\"x_max\"] - VM_PFC[\"x_min\"],\n                               VM_PFC[\"y_max\"] - VM_PFC[\"y_min\"],\n                               fill=False, edgecolor=\"cyan\", linewidth=1.0, linestyle=\"--\"))\n    axs[1, 0].hist(roi_mean, bins=12, color=\"#427AA1\", edgecolor=\"white\")\n    axs[1, 0].axvline(roi_mean_group, color=\"#C44536\", lw=2, label=\"group mean\")\n    axs[1, 0].axvline(0, color=\"black\", lw=1)\n    axs[1, 0].set_title(\"Participant mean estimates in vmPFC zone\")\n    axs[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Mean contrast estimate (arbitrary units)\")\n    axs[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"Participants\")\n    axs[1, 0].legend(frameon=False)\n    axs[1, 1].axis(\"off\")\n    axs[1, 1].text(0, 0.92,\n        \"Inference summary\\n\"\n        f\"N = {n}; exclusions = 0\\n\"\n        f\"Whole-brain max-T p = {p_max:.4g}\\n\"\n        f\"Whole-brain FWE voxels = {int(significant.sum())}\\n\"\n        f\"vmPFC-zone FWE voxels = {int(sig_roi.sum())}\\n\"\n        f\"vmPFC mean = {roi_mean_group:.4f} [95% CI {roi_ci[0]:.4f}, {roi_ci[1]:.4f}]\\n\"\n        f\"vmPFC-zone peak t = {t_obs[roi_peak_i]:.2f}\",\n        va=\"top\", fontsize=12, linespacing=1.7)\n    fig.suptitle(\"NARPS equal-indifference group: potential-gain effect\", fontsize=15)\n    fig.savefig(FIG / \"group_gain_effect.png\", dpi=180)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\n    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in result.items() if k != \"input_files\"}, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--permutations\", type=int, default=5000)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=20261016)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--chunk-size\", type=int, default=16)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    main(args.permutations, args.seed, args.chunk_size)\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n# Potential gains and brain activity\n\nDoes increasing potential monetary gain produce a greater fMRI response in the ventromedial prefrontal cortex (vmPFC) in the NARPS equal-indifference group?\n\nTest the hypothesis that this response increases with potential gain.\nParticipants performed a mixed-gambles task, deciding whether to accept gambles with possible gains and losses.\nIn this group, the range of potential gains was twice the range of potential losses.\n\nInvestigate the question at the group-analysis stage using the supplied 54 participant gain-effect maps and metadata.\nPreprocessing and individual modeling are fixed inputs, described in `upstream-methods.md`; do not repeat them or download time-series scans.\nChoose scientifically defensible group models, quality checks, software and visualizations.\nAccount for what the supplied effect estimates measure and the limits of their upstream model.\nUse whole-brain correction for multiple comparisons when evaluating support for the hypothesis, as required by the original study; justify how you identify vmPFC.\n\nProduce a concise scientific report with informative figures and the code and results supporting your conclusions.\nExplain uncertainty, exclusions and limitations, including what a lack of support would mean.\nPrior teams' answers are not ground truth or a required result.\n\nSource: [NARPS original analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf).\n# Scientific assessment context\n\nAssess the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: a positive parametric effect of potential gain in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group.\nThe original [analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) require whole-brain-corrected inference.\nThe scientific task is in `input/study-task.md`.\n\nWorkers receive 54 participant gain-effect maps from team AO86 and the corresponding cohort metadata.\nPreprocessing and participant modeling are fixed; evaluate group inference conditional on those inputs.\nJudge whether the analysis handles the intended participants, image geometry, quality, gain scaling, uncertainty and anatomical interpretation appropriately.\nThe maps represent independent participants; runs have already been combined within each person.\nEvaluate exclusions, uncertainty and multiple-comparison correction against the actual method.\nDefensible approaches can reach different conclusions; matching a prior team's answer is not the criterion.\nKeep scientific validity separate from the frozen STAMPED assessment.\nCheck how image coverage and missing observations enter the analysis; whether spatial alignment, vmPFC definition, group-model assumptions and whole-brain correction support the claimed inference; and whether quality checks, uncertainty and figures make those decisions inspectable.\nDo not require a particular mask, atlas, model or numerical result.\nParticipant variance maps are absent; judge methods against the supplied data.\n--- stop inventory of key items ---\nreceipt_sha256=d3e36b3b599d2f9051f291dff8b9b684985533128423a1e859dd2669814eb57e\nworker {'pid': 30570, 'returncode': 0, 'stop_reason': 'exited', 'stopped_at': '2026-10-16T06:37:12.208107+00:00', 'timed_out': False}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/.gitignore\"; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" status --short --ignored; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" rev-parse HEAD; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" remote -v; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" config --local --get-regexp '\"'\"'^(remote'\"\\\\.|annex\\\\.|filter\\\\.|core\\\\.hooksPath)' || true; cat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/results.json\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/fwe_clusters.tsv\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/included_participants.tsv\" | head'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/.gitignore\"; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" status --short --ignored; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" rev-parse HEAD; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" remote -v; git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" config --local --get-regexp '\"'\"'^(remote'\"\\\\.|annex\\\\.|filter\\\\.|core\\\\.hooksPath)' || true; cat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/results.json\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/fwe_clusters.tsv\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/included_participants.tsv\" | head'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Run the pinned assessment helpers in their recorded Pixi environment.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom contextlib import chdir, nullcontext\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport assessment_procedure as procedure\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\n\ndef git(*args, cwd=ROOT):\n    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", *args], cwd=cwd)\n\n\ndef dispatch_directory(frozen):\n    \"\"\"Keep v4 relative helper paths inside its existing judgment workspace.\"\"\"\n    if not frozen or frozen.get(\"version\") != 4:\n        return ROOT\n    value = os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\")\n    if not value or not Path(value).is_absolute() or not Path(value).is_dir():\n        raise SystemExit(\"Version 4 requires an existing absolute STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT directory\")\n    output = Path(value).resolve()\n    if output == ROOT.resolve():\n        raise SystemExit(\"Version 4 judgment output must be separate from the coordinator root\")\n    target = os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\")\n    if target:\n        target = Path(target).resolve()\n        if output.is_relative_to(target) or target.is_relative_to(output):\n            raise SystemExit(\"Version 4 judgment output must be separate from the assessed target\")\n    return output\n\n\ndef captured_replay(arguments, helper, operational=False):\n    \"\"\"Replay documented outputs from a verified complete copy, never from HEAD.\"\"\"\n    import importlib.util\n    import signal\n    import time\n    from delivery_snapshot import materialize_capture, validate_capture\n\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=captured_replay.__doc__, allow_abbrev=False)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--path\", type=Path, required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--entry\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--outputs\", nargs=\"+\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--workdir\", type=Path, required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", type=Path, required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--rtol\", type=float, default=1e-6)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=7200)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--max-get-gb\", type=float, default=5.0)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--in-container\")\n    args = parser.parse_args(arguments)\n    manifest_path = Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\"])\n    receipt = json.loads(Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT\"]).read_bytes())\n    identity = validate_capture(manifest_path, receipt[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n    manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_bytes())\n    original = manifest_path.parent / manifest[\"workspace\"]\n    declared = Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\"]) if operational else original\n    procedure.require_equal(args.path.resolve(), declared.resolve(), \"captured replay source\")\n    report = {\"probe\": \"fresh-rerun\", \"source\": str(original), \"capture\": identity[\"capture\"],\n              \"commit\": identity[\"commit\"], \"captured_at\": identity[\"captured_at\"],\n              \"scope\": \"Complete stopped delivery copy; existing environment/cache bytes retained. \"\n                       \"One documented entrypoint, no repair or automatic retrieval; selected outputs only.\",\n              \"entry\": args.entry, \"outputs\": args.outputs, \"rtol\": args.rtol}\n    if operational:\n        report[\"retrieval_scope\"] = {\n            \"adapter_input_retrieval\": \"none; uses captured inputs\",\n            \"entrypoint_network_byte_limit\": None,\n            \"entrypoint_downloads\": \"Documented dependency installs/downloads are not byte-metered\",\n            \"max_get_gb\": args.max_get_gb,\n            \"max_get_gb_scope\": \"Frozen helper-prefetch compatibility parameter; this adapter performs no prefetch\",\n        }\n    def finish(status, reason):\n        report.update(status=status, reason=reason)\n        validate_capture(manifest_path, identity[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n        args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        with args.output.open(\"x\") as stream:\n            json.dump(report, stream, indent=2)\n            stream.write(\"\\n\")\n        print(json.dumps(report))\n        return 0\n    observations = [row[\"path\"] for row in manifest.get(\"declared_artifacts\", [])\n                    if isinstance(row.get(\"declaration\"), dict) and\n                    row[\"declaration\"].get(\"kind\") == \"native-session-skill-directory\"]\n    # Skills installed in the native profile are retained observation evidence,\n    # not scientific execution dependencies. A workspace link to one opts it in.\n    referenced = set()\n    for row in manifest[\"entries\"]:\n        if row[\"path\"].startswith(\"content/workspace/\") and row[\"kind\"] == \"symlink\":\n            try:\n                target = (manifest_path.parent / row[\"path\"]).resolve()\n                referenced.update(prefix for prefix in observations\n                                  if target.is_relative_to(manifest_path.parent / prefix))\n            except (OSError, RuntimeError):\n                pass\n    observations = [prefix for prefix in observations if prefix not in referenced]\n    def execution_evidence(row):\n        return not any(row[\"path\"] == prefix or row[\"path\"].startswith(prefix + \"/\")\n                       for prefix in observations)\n    issues = manifest.get(\"errors\", []) + manifest.get(\"omissions\", [])\n    report[\"observation_only_capture_issues\"] = [row for row in issues if not execution_evidence(row)]\n    if any(execution_evidence(row) for row in issues):\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Scientific execution capture has explicit omissions or errors; no replay executed.\")\n    if args.in_container:\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"This bounded adapter does not relocate container bindings.\")\n    if not args.entry.strip() or any(not value.strip() or Path(value).is_absolute() or\n                                   \"..\" in Path(value).parts for value in args.outputs):\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Entrypoint and repository-relative generated output patterns are required.\")\n    if any(execution_evidence(row) for row in manifest.get(\"git_dependencies\", [])):\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Original external Git pointers are retained as evidence, not relocated for execution.\")\n    for row in manifest[\"entries\"]:\n        if row[\"kind\"] == \"symlink\" and execution_evidence(row):\n            link = manifest_path.parent / row[\"path\"]\n            try:\n                inside = link.resolve().is_relative_to(manifest_path.parent.resolve())\n            except (OSError, RuntimeError):\n                inside = False\n            if not inside or Path(os.readlink(link)).is_absolute():\n                return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Original links outside the captured copy cannot be safely replayed without relocation.\")\n    materialized = materialize_capture(manifest_path, args.workdir)\n    clone = Path(materialized[\"target\"])\n    report[\"workdir\"] = str(clone)\n    # Comparison semantics come from the exact frozen assessor, in its runtime.\n    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"frozen_fresh_rerun\", helper)\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    protected = {row[\"path\"] for row in receipt.get(\"seed_identities\", {}).get(\"supplied_files\", [])}\n    before = module._collect(clone, args.outputs)\n    code_suffixes = {\".py\", \".sh\", \".r\", \".m\", \".ipynb\", \".jl\", \".toml\", \".lock\", \".yaml\", \".yml\"}\n    for path in before:\n        selected = clone / path\n        if (path in protected or Path(path).parts[0] in (\"input\", \".git\", \".codex\", \".entire\", \".agents\") or\n                selected.suffix.lower() in code_suffixes or selected.name in (\"Makefile\", \"Dockerfile\") or\n                not selected.resolve().is_relative_to(clone.resolve())):\n            return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Output selection includes supplied inputs, code/configuration, or external content: \" + path)\n    if not before or any(digest is None for digest in before.values()):\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"No complete generated output payload matches the explicit selection.\")\n    report[\"original_output_sha256\"] = before\n    for path in before:\n        (clone / path).unlink()\n    report[\"removed_outputs\"] = sorted(before)\n    command = [\"sh\", \"-c\", args.entry]\n    started = time.monotonic()\n    with (args.workdir / \"replay.stdout\").open(\"xb\") as stdout, (args.workdir / \"replay.stderr\").open(\"xb\") as stderr:\n        environment = os.environ.copy()\n        if operational:\n            environment = procedure.git_config_overlay(procedure.operational_environment(environment),\n                                                        {\"core.hooksPath\": os.devnull})\n            environment[\"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\"] = \"1\"\n        else:\n            environment.update(GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=\"0\", PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=\"1\",\n                               GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=\"1\", GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=\"core.hooksPath\", GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=os.devnull)\n        report[\"replay_git_overlay\"] = {\"core.hooksPath\": os.devnull,\n            \"reason\": \"Disable original checkout hooks in the replay copy; captured config bytes unchanged\"}\n        process = subprocess.Popen(command, cwd=clone, env=environment, stdout=stdout, stderr=stderr,\n                                   start_new_session=True)\n        try:\n            code = process.wait(timeout=args.timeout)\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            os.killpg(process.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n            process.wait()\n            code = 124\n            report[\"timed_out\"] = True\n    report.update(returncode=code, elapsed_seconds=time.monotonic() - started,\n                  stdout=str(args.workdir / \"replay.stdout\"), stderr=str(args.workdir / \"replay.stderr\"))\n    if report.get(\"timed_out\"):\n        return finish(\"not-checked\", \"Frozen replay time limit reached; evidence retained, replay incomplete.\")\n    if code:\n        return finish(\"unmet\", \"Documented entrypoint failed in the complete delivery copy; interpret within the recorded environment scope.\")\n    after = module._collect(clone, args.outputs)\n    identical, close, differing, missing = [], [], [], []\n    for path, digest in before.items():\n        if after.get(path) is None:\n            missing.append(path)\n        elif after[path] == digest:\n            identical.append(path)\n        elif path.endswith(module.TABLE_SUFFIXES) and module._numeric_close(original / path, clone / path, args.rtol):\n            close.append(path)\n        else:\n            differing.append(path)\n    report[\"comparison\"] = {\"identical\": identical, \"within_tolerance\": close,\n                            \"differing\": differing, \"missing_after_rerun\": missing}\n    if differing or missing:\n        return finish(\"partial\" if identical or close else \"unmet\", \"Some selected generated outputs did not reproduce.\")\n    return finish(\"met\", \"All selected generated outputs were recreated within the frozen comparison tolerance.\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"check\", \"probes\", \"response\", \"validate\", \"fresh-rerun\"))\n    parser.add_argument(\"arguments\", nargs=argparse.REMAINDER)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    remaining = args.arguments\n    pin_path = Path(os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PIN\", ROOT / \"assessment-version.json\"))\n    pin = json.loads(pin_path.read_text())\n    frozen_path = os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_PROCEDURE\")\n    frozen = None\n    if frozen_path:\n        frozen = procedure.load_procedure(frozen_path, os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_PROCEDURE_SHA256\"))\n        procedure.require_equal(pin, frozen[\"assessment\"], \"assessment runner pin\")\n        procedure.require_equal(procedure.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()),\n                                frozen[\"fixed_files\"][\"scripts/assessment.py\"], \"assessment runner source\")\n    operational = bool(frozen and frozen.get(\"version\") == 4)\n    dispatch_cwd = dispatch_directory(frozen)\n    source = Path(os.environ.get(\"STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_SOURCE\", ROOT / \"assessment\"))\n    if operational:\n        source = source.resolve()\n    if git(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\", cwd=source).decode().strip() != pin[\"source_commit\"]:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Assessment checkout differs from the frozen version\")\n    if git(\"status\", \"--porcelain\", cwd=source).strip():\n        raise SystemExit(\"Assessment checkout has local changes\")\n    if not procedure.assessment_modules_match(git(\"submodule\", \"status\", \"--recursive\", cwd=source)):\n        raise SystemExit(\"Assessment submodules are not at their recorded revisions\")\n    revision = pin[\"environment_commit\"]\n    repository = pin.get(\"environment_repository\", \"origin\")\n    if not isinstance(repository, str) or not repository.strip():\n        raise SystemExit(\"Assessment environment_repository must name a Git repository or remote\")\n    if subprocess.run([\"git\", \"cat-file\", \"-e\", revision], cwd=ROOT, capture_output=True).returncode:\n        subprocess.run([\"git\", \"fetch\", \"--no-tags\", \"--depth\", \"1\", repository, revision],\n                       cwd=ROOT, check=True)\n    runtime = ROOT / \".pixi\" / \"assessment-runtime\" / revision\n    runtime.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for name in (\"pixi.toml\", \"pixi.lock\"):\n        content = git(\"show\", f\"{revision}:{name}\")\n        if hashlib.sha256(content).hexdigest() != pin[\"sha256\"][name]:\n            raise SystemExit(f\"Frozen {name} hash differs\")\n        target = runtime / name\n        if target.exists() and target.read_bytes() != content:\n            raise SystemExit(f\"Recorded environment was changed locally: {target}\")\n        target.write_bytes(content)\n    manifest = runtime / \"pixi.toml\"\n    if operational:\n        manifest = manifest.resolve()\n    subprocess.run([\"pixi\", \"install\", \"--locked\", \"--manifest-path\", manifest], check=True)\n    if args.action == \"check\":\n        if remaining:\n            parser.error(\"check takes no additional arguments\")\n        print(json.dumps(pin, indent=2))\n        return\n    scripts = source / \"skills\" / \"assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\" / \"scripts\"\n    if args.action in (\"response\", \"validate\"):\n        helper = source / \"skills\" / \"stamped-conventions\" / \"scripts\" / \"encode_response.py\"\n        if args.action == \"validate\":\n            remaining.insert(0, \"validate\")\n    else:\n        helper = scripts / {\"probes\": \"run_probes.py\", \"fresh-rerun\": \"fresh_rerun.py\"}[args.action]\n    if frozen and args.action == \"fresh-rerun\":\n        target = Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\"])\n        if procedure.is_neutral(frozen):\n            # Validate relative replay paths in the same directory the adapter\n            # will use, even when the runner was invoked from the target.\n            with chdir(dispatch_cwd) if operational else nullcontext():\n                remaining = procedure.replay_arguments(frozen, remaining, target,\n                                                       Path(os.environ[\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\"]))\n            result = subprocess.run([\"pixi\", \"run\", \"--locked\", \"--manifest-path\", manifest,\ncat: /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/operational/content/workspace/.gitignore: No such file or directory\n?? .task_skills/\n?? analysis.py\n?? analysis_notebook.ipynb\n?? report.md\n?? results/\n!! .codex/\n!! .entire/\ne929d623d8de313d2ecdd97911ea8487077af580\ncore.hookspath /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/workspaces/narps-neutral-r1-12/.git/hooks\nannex.uuid 90af5845-6a95-46f6-9f2b-60406cbef165\nannex.version 10\nfilter.annex.smudge git-annex smudge -- %f\nfilter.annex.clean git-annex smudge --clean -- %f\nfilter.annex.process git-annex filter-process\n{\n  \"n_participants\": 54,\n  \"n_excluded\": 0,\n  \"map_checksums_verified\": 54,\n  \"grid_shape\": [\n    97,\n    115,\n    81\n  ],\n  \"voxel_size_mm\": [\n    2.0,\n    2.0,\n    2.4000000953674316\n  ],\n  \"common_support_voxels\": 198029,\n  \"common_support_volume_ml\": 1901.0784755420684,\n  \"vmPFC_coordinate_box_MNI_mm\": {\n    \"x_min\": -20,\n    \"x_max\": 20,\n    \"y_min\": 20,\n    \"y_max\": 60,\n    \"z_min\": -20,\n    \"z_max\": 20\n  },\n  \"vmPFC_voxels\": 7043,\n  \"vmPFC_mean_cope\": -0.0004832247591900498,\n  \"vmPFC_mean_cope_95pct_t_CI\": [\n    -0.014309229093454605,\n    0.013342779575074504\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_peak_t\": 4.1918477635940805,\n  \"vmPFC_peak_xyz_MNI_mm\": [\n    -2.0,\n    24.0,\n    -17.99999761581421\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_FWE_significant_voxels\": 0,\n  \"whole_brain_peak_t\": 6.