{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response items > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-items.txt\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-items.stderr\"; printf '\"'items_exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$?\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-items.txt\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-items.stderr\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes.json\"'","aggregated_output":"items_exit=0\nstamped-checklist:must/001\tmust\tS.1\tAre all files and directories nested under a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/002\tmust\tS.1\tAre datasets included, linked, or referenced reachable from the code and environment specifications without crossing the boundary of a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/003\tmust\tS.1\tIs external software included in the environment or linked as submodules within the project boundary?\nstamped-checklist:must/004\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `Git` used for code, text, documentation, and configuration files?\nstamped-checklist:must/005\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `git-annex`, DataLad, or `Git` LFS used for large binary data?\nstamped-checklist:must/006\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\n{\n  \"checklist_version\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"responses\": {\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/001\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No probe covers this item; a reading of the object is required.\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"source\": \"judgement\",\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"stamped-checklist:must/002\": {\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"No submodules or subdatasets: whether external inputs are linked at all needs a reading of the object.\",\n      \