                            [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}]\n                                [--dependency DEPENDENCY] [--capture CAPTURE]\n                                response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --harness HARNESS     e.g. \"claude-code (subagent)\"\n  --model MODEL\n  --scope SCOPE         what this assessment did and did not cover\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n                        the object's kind (see references/project-kinds.md)\n  --dependency DEPENDENCY\n                        e.g. \"stamped-conventions@0.1.0\"; repeatable\n  --capture CAPTURE     hash a retained delivery manifest/archive; preserve\n                        any recorded Git commit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py encode [-h] [--base-url BASE_URL] [--allow-invalid]\n                                 response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  --base-url BASE_URL\n  --allow-invalid      encode even if validation fails\n{\n  \"n_participants\": 54,\n  \"n_excluded\": 0,\n  \"map_checksums_verified\": 54,\n  \"grid_shape\": [\n    97,\n    115,\n    81\n  ],\n  \"voxel_size_mm\": [\n    2.0,\n    2.0,\n    2.4000000953674316\n  ],\n  \"common_support_voxels\": 198029,\n  \"common_support_volume_ml\": 1901.0784755420684,\n  \"vmPFC_coordinate_box_MNI_mm\": {\n    \"x_min\": -20,\n    \"x_max\": 20,\n    \"y_min\": 20,\n    \"y_max\": 60,\n    \"z_min\": -20,\n    \"z_max\": 20\n  },\n  \"vmPFC_voxels\": 7043,\n  \"vmPFC_mean_cope\": -0.0004832247591900498,\n  \"vmPFC_mean_cope_95pct_t_CI\": [\n    -0.014309229093454605,\n    0.013342779575074504\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_peak_t\": 4.1918477635940805,\n  \"vmPFC_peak_xyz_MNI_mm\": [\n    -2.0,\n    24.0,\n    -17.99999761581421\n  ],\n  \"vmPFC_FWE_significant_voxels\": 0,\n  \"whole_brain_peak_t\": 6.617173246302241,\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/operational/content/workspace/analysis.py\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/operational/content/workspace/analysis_notebook.ipynb\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/operational/content/workspace/report.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\" | sed -n '\"'1,38p'; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\np=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nfor path in ['content/workspace/report.md','content/workspace/analysis.py','content/workspace/results/results.json','content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md','content/workspace/input/participants.tsv','content/workspace/input/sources.json','content/workspace/analysis_notebook.ipynb']:\n x=next((e for e in p['entries'] if e.get('path')==path),None); print(path, x and x.get('sha256'), x and x.get('mode'))\nprint('head_commit',p['head_commit'])\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-runner-2.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-runner-2.stderr\"; find \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print | sort'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\" | sed -n '\"'1,38p'; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\np=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nfor path in ['content/workspace/report.md','content/workspace/analysis.py','content/workspace/results/results.json','content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md','content/workspace/input/participants.tsv','content/workspace/input/sources.json','content/workspace/analysis_notebook.ipynb']:\n x=next((e for e in p['entries'] if e.get('path')==path),None); print(path, x and x.get('sha256'), x and x.get('mode'))\nprint('head_commit',p['head_commit'])\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-runner-2.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-runner-2.stderr\"; find \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print | sort'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Potential gain and brain activity in the NARPS equal-indifference group\n     2\t\n     3\t## Question and result\n     4\t\n     5\tWe tested the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: whether greater potential gains are associated with a positive fMRI response in ventromedial prefrontal cortex (vmPFC) in the equal-indifference group. A whole-brain, one-sided max-statistic permutation test found corrected positive effects somewhere in the brain (peak *t*(53) = 6.62, MNI [−26, −102, −4], max-T FWE *p* = .0010; 24 voxels exceeded the corrected threshold). However, no whole-brain FWE-significant voxels fell in the prespecified vmPFC territory. The vmPFC-zone peak was *t*(53) = 4.19, below the whole-brain critical *t* = 5.40. Thus, this analysis does **not** support the specific vmPFC hypothesis, although it detects a positive effect elsewhere.\n     6\t\n     7\t![Group gain-effect results](results/figures/group_gain_effect.png)\n     8\t\n     9\t## Data and model\n    10\t\n    11\tWe analyzed all 54 equal-indifference participants listed in the supplied cohort table. In this mixed-gambles group, the potential-gain range was twice the potential-loss range. Their maps are unthresholded participant-level gain contrast parameter estimates from AO86, averaged across four runs and reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space. All 54 files matched the supplied SHA-256 checksums, had finite values, and shared the same 97 × 115 × 81 voxel grid (2 × 2 × 2.4 mm). No participants were excluded. Because zero-valued voxels denote locations outside a participant’s estimation support, the group test used only the intersection of nonzero map support (198,029 voxels; 1,901 ml); this avoids interpreting absent estimates as observed zero effects. The masks are saved in `results/`. We did not reprocess scans or download time-series data.\n    12\t\n    13\tAt each voxel, we estimated the group mean and a one-sample random-effects *t* statistic across participant contrast estimates, testing the prespecified positive direction. Whole-brain familywise error was controlled with 5,000 participant-level sign-flip permutations of the maximum voxelwise *t* statistic (seed 20261016). The 95th percentile of the permutation maximum distribution was *t* = 5.397. This makes the brain-wide test primary and uses a directional test consistent with the original hypothesis. A finite permutation sample gives a minimum reportable *p* of 1/5,001.\n    14\t\n    15\tWe labeled vmPFC in advance as a medial anterior ventral prefrontal coordinate zone in MNI space (x −20 to 20, y 20 to 60, z −20 to 20 mm). This transparent anatomical approximation only labels the corrected whole-brain result; it does not reduce the number of tested voxels or provide a separate uncorrected ROI claim. The zone contained 7,043 tested voxels. Its mean estimate was −0.00048 (95% *t* interval −0.0143 to 0.0133, in arbitrary contrast-estimate units); its largest voxelwise *t* was 4.19 and none of its voxels passed whole-brain FWE correction.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Interpretation and limits\n    18\t\n    19\tThe direction of evidence in the vmPFC zone is not sufficient to establish a positive gain response. Failure to pass whole-brain correction is not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero: it means this sample and fixed analysis do not provide sufficiently strong spatially specific evidence under the required whole-brain criterion. The near-zero zone average is descriptive and can conceal spatially heterogeneous effects.\n    20\t\n    21\tThese inputs are contrast estimates, not standardized statistics; upstream gain values were mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution, so coefficients cannot be read as signal change per currency unit. The individual models used response-time durations and separate gain and loss models, making the estimate conditional on that model and not a direct causal effect of currency value. Individual variance maps and the full upstream executable pipeline are unavailable, so we could not propagate first-level uncertainty through a summary-statistics model or re-evaluate upstream modeling choices. Group inference treats the participant maps as estimates with between-participant variation. The sign-flip max-T method relies on exchangeability/symmetry under the null. The common-support mask is conservative at varying edges and may affect sensitivity. Finally, vmPFC boundaries are not uniquely defined; the coordinate-zone rule is a reproducible approximation, while the primary correction appropriately covers the full brain.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Reproducibility\n    24\t\n    25\tRun `python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016` from the workspace root using the supplied Python environment. The script verifies input checksums and writes maps, masks, numerical output, and the figure into `results/`. `analysis_notebook.ipynb` documents and reruns the workflow. `results/results.json` contains the full machine-readable summary and input checksums.\n    26\t\n    27\tThe one-sided, whole-brain inference requirement follows the [NARPS original analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf), which predicts a positive vmPFC effect for the equal-indifference group and asks teams for whole-brain corrected results. The original NARPS paper likewise states that the hypotheses should be reported from whole-brain rather than ROI-only analyses ([Botvinik-Nezer et al., 2020](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-020-2314-9)).\ncontent/workspace/report.md 56040611387d9a12b06f9c50fae9a66b7757af4664c61fee65b10a5ba4f75be0 420\ncontent/workspace/analysis.py 62b32a0086ec516fa7e83bc9f0fa0594c58224d6466aefe184e859e01247ee5a 420\ncontent/workspace/results/results.json 7a6ffaa9ce46f2087054449fcacc402be3b18c20fa5eed74bc5d9cc2ce6fc5c2 420\ncontent/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md 508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b 420\ncontent/workspace/input/participants.tsv faca815bcb042144bdb8dcff915f45de0d27650f60416ed76a5a72557341abbf 420\ncontent/workspace/input/sources.json 919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd 420\ncontent/workspace/analysis_notebook.ipynb 795f608c7934b60b7771bc61c41f4275df32ecf304bbc6060493e6f6037c89df 420\nhead_commit e929d623d8de313d2ecdd97911ea8487077af580\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nFormal replay allowance already consumed; retain this attempt\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.codex/hooks.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.entire/.gitignore\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.entire/settings.local.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.git/config\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.git/HEAD\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.git/index\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/.gitignore\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/checklist-items.stderr\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/checklist-items.txt\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/formal-replay-attempt.json\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/inspection-git-head.txt\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-12-j01/attempt-01/judgment/inspection-git-remotes.txt\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neu