{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build_assessment.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nout=Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\ntarget=Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET'])\nmanifest=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\ncapture='783faf61b2b84a56c1a82f46c5dceb88ecba15be11981f2c55870311f89e09c9'\ncommit=manifest['head_commit']\nentries={e['path']:e for e in manifest['entries']}\ndef ev(path, description):\n p='content/workspace/'+path\n row=entries.get(p,{})\n return {'uri':f'capture:sha256:{capture}#{p}','description':description,'sha256':row.get('sha256')}\nresponses={\n'must/001':('met','All retained workspace material, including Git and annex data, is nested under the single workspace root.',[ev('input/participants.tsv','Participant metadata is inside the workspace root'),ev('analysis.py','Analysis source is inside the workspace root')]),\n'must/002':('met','The code uses paths relative to its own workspace and the 54 supplied input maps are retained inside the project through annex objects; no external pointer is required.',[ev('analysis.py','ROOT-relative input/output paths'),ev('input/sources.json','Input map checksum and source mapping'),ev('input/participants.tsv','Cohort metadata')]),\n'must/003':('unmet','The analysis imports external Python packages (NumPy, SciPy, pandas, nibabel, matplotlib) but no environment declaration or bundled/submodule software supplies them.',[ev('analysis.py','External package imports'),ev('report.md','Run instruction only says “supplied Python environment”; no reproducible environment specification')]),\n'must/004':('unmet','At worker stop, the analysis, notebook, report, and result directory were untracked. The committed HEAD therefore did not version the delivered research code, documentation, or results.',[ev('analysis.py','Untracked at worker stop according to captured Git status'),ev('report.md','Untracked at worker stop according to captured Git status'),ev('analysis_notebook.ipynb','Untracked at worker stop according to captured Git status')]),\n'must/005':('met','The 54 supplied image maps are tracked through git-annex pointers with retained annex payloads; the frozen probe found no binary Git blob over 10 MiB.',[ev('input/sources.json','54 input map identities and checksums'),ev('input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz','Representative retained annex-backed participant map')]),\n'must/006':('unmet','The result record lists several package versions but does not include an exact environment specification linked to the run, and the delivered results were untracked at worker stop.',[ev('results/results.json','Software versions are reported, but no exact package/environment lock is recorded'),ev('analysis.py','Run implementation and outputs')]),\n'must/007':('unmet','There is no README.md or Makefile with installation and usage instructions. The report gives a run command, but does not satisfy the specified README/Makefile artifact requirement.',[ev('report.md','Run command appears under Reproducibility; no README or Makefile exists at workspace root')]),\n'must/008':('met','The complete stopped delivery has a clear entrypoint: the report directs the reader to run analysis.py from the workspace root, with the required permutation and seed arguments.',[ev('report.md','Documented command: python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016'),ev('analysis.py','Runnable analysis entrypoint')]),\n'must/009':('met','The analysis constructs input and output paths relative to the script location; the report uses relative artifact links.',[ev('analysis.py','Path(__file__).resolve().parent defines ROOT; inputs and outputs are relative'),ev('report.md','Relative results figure link')]),\n'must/010':('unmet','No dependency/environment specification is supplied; the documented “supplied Python environment” is not identified or reconstructible from worker-declared files.',[ev('report.md','Environment is referenced but not identified'),ev('analysis.py','Imports required external packages')]),\n'must/011':('unmet','The report and code do not document the host operating system, system libraries, or other host assumptions needed to run the analysis.',[ev('report.md','No host requirements are specified'),ev('analysis.py','Python package imports do not describe host prerequisites')]),\n'must/012':('unmet','There is no clear list of runtime dependencies or system requirements in a README or environment specification.',[ev('report.md','Only an unspecified supplied Python environment is mentioned'),ev('analysis.py','Imports reveal dependencies but do not declare installation requirements')]),\n'must/013':('unmet','No environment specification is included in version control or in the complete stopped delivery.',[ev('analysis.py','Analysis source; no environment file accompanies it'),ev('report.md','No pinned environment declared')]),\n'must/014':('unmet','No environment specification or documented process for updating one is present.',[ev('report.md','No environment maintenance process'),ev('analysis.py','No dependency specification')]),\n'must/015':('unmet','No frozen package manifest, container digest, or equivalent exact environment artifact is supplied.',[ev('report.md','Unspecified supplied Python environment'),ev('results/results.json','Only selected software versions, not a full pinned environment')]),\n'must/016':('unmet','No worker-supplied environment specification is available to share through an authorized route.',[ev('report.md','No shareable environment specification identified')]),\n'must/017':('unmet','The report provides no instructions for obtaining or using an environment specification because none is supplied.',[ev('report.md','Run command refers only to an unspecified supplied Python environment')]),\n'should/001':('unmet','A Git repository is present, but the delivered code, report, notebook, and result artifacts were untracked at worker stop; a common VCS therefore does not cover all components.',[ev('analysis.py','Untracked delivered code'),ev('report.md','Untracked delivered report')]),\n'should/002':('not-checked','No evidence establishes regular testing over time. The absence of recognized CI configuration is not enough to rule out other testing records, and none were identified.',[ev('analysis.py','Single documented workflow; no repeated-test evidence')]),\n'should/003':('partial','Inputs and generated results have separate directories, but code sits at the root and no environment module exists.',[ev('input/participants.tsv','Inputs are grouped under input/'),ev('results/results.json','Derived outputs grouped under results/'),ev('analysis.py','Code remains at workspace root')]),\n'should/004':('not-checked','No evidence shows routine execution in a fresh container, batch job, clean VM, or cloud instance.',[ev('report.md','No fresh-environment testing record')]),\n'should/005':('not-checked','No disposable-environment workflow is documented or recorded.',[ev('report.md','No disposable execution environment described')]),\n'should/006':('unmet','There is no exact environment specification to test for reconstitution.',[ev('report.md','No environment specification supplied')]),\n'should/007':('unmet','No environment artifact is archived in the research object.',[ev('report.md','No environment artifact identified')]),\n'should/008':('unmet','No environment specification or process for updating and tracking one is supplied.',[ev('report.md','No environment update process')]),\n'should/009':('not-checked','The delivery does not identify restricted data or software, so whether any restricted material needed separate modular handling cannot be determined.',[ev('input/sources.json','Sources are identified; no access restriction is declared')]),\n'may/001':('not-applicable','The workspace has no independently maintained submodule or subdataset component to compose; inputs are included as annex-backed files.',[ev('input/sources.json','Inputs are included in the workspace rather than linked as a submodule')]),\n'may/002':('not-applicable','No recombinable modular structure is present; the delivery is one small analysis workspace.',[ev('report.md','Describes one analysis and its input/results folders')]),\n'may/003':('not-applicable','There are no separately maintained modules with independent update boundaries.',[ev('analysis.py','Single analysis script')]),\n'may/004':('not-applicable','There are no independent modules requiring a composition mechanism.',[ev('report.md','One workspace-level command')]),\n'may/005':('partial','The report and notebook point to the main analysis and result artifacts, but no README or navigation guide explains the workspace structure.',[ev('report.md','Explains entrypoint, results, and interpretation'),ev('analysis_notebook.ipynb','Notebook documents workflow')]),\n}\nresponse=json.load(open(out/'response.json'))\nfor key,(status,reason,evidence) in responses.items():\n item='stamped-checklist:'+key\n row=response['responses'][item]\n row['status']=status\n row['value']={'met':'yes','unmet':'no','partial':'no','not-applicable':None,'not-checked':None}[status]\n row['reason']=reason\n row['evidence']=evidence\n row['source']='judgement'\n# Keep canonical object identity and original HEAD.\nresponse['object']={'url':None,'commit':commit,'captured_at':manifest['captured_at'],'kind':'study'}\nresponse['scope']='Independent assessment of the complete operational copy against canonical capture; scientific review, frozen probes, worker-stop attribution, and one permitted captured-delivery replay workflow (blocked before scientific execution).'\nresponse['assessor']={'skill':'assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles','version':'0.1.0','harness':'Codex','model':'gpt-6.1-sol','date':'2026-10-16','drafted_by':'judgement'}\n(out/'response.json').write_text(json.dumps(response,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nreport='''# Independent assessment report\n\n## Scope and identity\n\nThis assessment covers the complete operational copy at worker stop, including uncommitted and ignored material. The canonical capture identity is SHA-256 \"'`783faf61b2b84a56c1a82f46c5dceb88ecba15be11981f2c55870311f89e09c9`; its captured HEAD is `e929d623d8de313d2ecdd97911ea8487077af580`. The canonical and operational manifests identify the same capture. Evidence citations below use canonical capture-relative paths rooted at `content/workspace/`; file digests are recorded in the response evidence entries.\n\nThe supplied worker-stop receipt identifies a successful worker exit and the same original HEAD. At stop, `analysis.py`, `analysis_notebook.ipynb`, `report.md`, `results/`, and `.task_skills/` were untracked; `.codex/` and `.entire/` were ignored. The result/code/report artifacts therefore existed in the complete stopped delivery but were not preserved by the recorded Git commit. The assessment found no configured Git remote or worker-declared retrieval route. Later coordinator capture, retention, and delivery do not establish worker publication or accessibility.\n\n## Scientific adequacy\n\n**Adequacy: supported. Hypothesis outcome: no support for the specific vmPFC hypothesis under this analysis.** The report analyzes all 54 intended participants without exclusions; describes checksum, finite-value, grid, and common-support checks; uses one-sample participant-level inference with a directional max-T permutation correction across the tested brain volume; and identifies vmPFC with an explicit coordinate-zone rule while retaining whole-brain correction. It reports no whole-brain-FWE-significant voxels in that zone, with a near-zero zone mean and interval, and correctly limits the interpretation to insufficient spatially specific evidence rather than evidence of an exact null.\n\nThe reported positive corrected effects elsewhere do not establish the vmPFC hypothesis. The estimate units are correctly treated as arbitrary first-level contrast units rather than signal per currency unit. The report acknowledges the missing participant variance maps, fixed upstream model, sign-flip exchangeability/symmetry assumption, conservative common-support mask, and approximate vmPFC boundary. Those limitations reduce sensitivity and constrain generalization but do not invalidate the bounded conclusion that this analysis did not support a corrected vmPFC effect.\n\nThe relevant report statement is: “Thus, this analysis does **not** support the specific vmPFC hypothesis, although it detects a positive effect elsewhere.” (`content/workspace/report.md`, line 5.) The reasoning is: “Failure to pass whole-brain correction is not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero: it means this sample and fixed analysis do not provide sufficiently strong spatially specific evidence under the required whole-brain criterion.” (`content/workspace/report.md`, line 19.) Both excerpts are quoted verbatim here for the required scientific record.\n\nKey artifacts: `analysis.py` implements checksum and geometry validation, common-support selection, the one-sided max-T procedure, and output generation; `results/results.json` records the numerical summary; `results/fwe_clusters.tsv` and `results/fwe_significant_voxels.tsv` expose corrected findings; `results/figures/group_gain_effect.png` visualizes the map, corrected voxels, and participant vmPFC averages. These are original captured artifacts, cited by canonical capture identity above.\n\n## Replay and measurement availability\n\nThe declared entrypoint was `python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016`. The explicit generated-output selection covered the ten files under `results/` plus `results/figures/group_gain_effect.png`; supplied `input/`, source code, and Git metadata were protected. The intended comparison was the frozen helper'\"'s \"'`rtol=1e-6` comparison for numerical outputs, with exact checks for nonnumeric outputs and no scientific equivalence claim for timestamps/log prose/formatting. Prerequisite reconstruction was limited to worker-supplied declarations; none identifies a complete environment.\n\nReplay is **not checked**. The first helper invocation failed before materialization because I had created the requested workdir in advance, whereas the helper requires a new destination. The failed command and traceback are retained in `replay-runner.stdout` and `.stderr`; the wrapper then recorded `formal-replay-attempt.json`. A subsequent valid invocation was rejected by the wrapper with “Formal replay allowance already consumed,” before creating a copy or running target code. Its command and output are retained in `replay-runner-2.stdout` and `.stderr`. This is an invocation/assessor-workflow limitation, not evidence about target behavior; no replay output was generated and no replay comparison is claimed.\n\n## Access and attribution\n\nIntended recipient: a researcher using the worker-declared authorized route. Worker-declared route: none found; the operational checkout has no Git remote. Required coverage would include the report, code, generated results, cohort metadata, and all 54 input maps. Tested host scope: local inspection environment only. The coordinator'\"'s preserved copy allowed this assessment but is not proof that the worker made the work accessible to another researcher. Worker version control and publication are judged at the recorded stop state; later coordinator retention receives no worker-practice credit.\n\n## STAMPED evidence and checklist\n\nThe item-level verdicts, reasons, and canonical capture/hash evidence are in \"'`response.json`; automated outputs are retained in `probes.json`. Probe outputs were interpreted against the full workspace: in particular, the frozen entrypoint probe only scanned tracked paths and missed the delivered untracked `analysis.py`, while complete-delivery inspection confirmed the report'\"'s documented command. No overall score is assigned. The checklist link is recorded in \"'`checklist-url.txt`.\n\nMaterial gaps include the untracked research deliverables, absent environment/dependency specification, absent README/Makefile, and absent worker-declared access route. The supplied input maps are annex-backed. Relative paths and a documented analysis command support portability/actionability within the limits of the missing environment declaration.\n\n## Exposure and assumptions\n\nThe stop capture contains `.entire/` interaction metadata and a `.task_skills/jupyter-notebook/` artifact. Their identifiers indicate an assistance/tool exposure; their contents were not used as grading evidence, and no treatment assignment is inferred or reported. Initial supplied guidance is treated as coordinator material per the receipt; later worker-installed resources are not credited as scientific evidence.\n\nAssumption: the captured annex payload mapping is the retained source for the supplied participant maps; no external pointer was followed. The runner'\"'s canonical capture identity is used for all source citations. Operational inspection artifacts (including Git status) are observations made during assessment and are not worker evidence.\n'''\n(out/'assessment-report.md').write_text(report)\n# Access record\naccess={'schema_version':1,'delivery_capture_sha256':capture,'recipient':'Researcher using the worker-declared authorized route','worker_declared_route':None,'route_status':'No worker-declared authorized retrieval route was found; no Git remote is configured.','required_artifact_coverage':['report.md','analysis.py','analysis_notebook.ipynb','results/','input/participants.tsv','input/sources.json','all 54 input/data/*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz maps'],'tested_host_scope':'Local assessment environment only, via the operational copy; no worker route or remote host was tested.','coordinator_delivery_is_worker_access_evidence':False}\n(out/'access-record.json').write_text(json.dumps(access,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\n# Replay record retains helper failure and wrapper guard; no scientific code ran.\nreplay={'schema_version':1,'delivery_capture_sha256':capture,'commit':commit,'status':'not-checked','entrypoint':'python analysis.py --permutations 5000 --seed 20261016','prerequisites':'No worker-supplied environment specification; no reconstruction or repair performed.','outputs':['results/group_mean_cope.nii.gz','results/group_t_map.nii.gz','results/voxelwise_fwe_p.nii.gz','results/fwe_significant_mask.nii.gz','results/common_support_mask.nii.gz','results/permutation_max_t.npy','results/fwe_clusters.tsv','results/fwe_significant_voxels.tsv','results/results.json','results/included_participants.tsv','results/figures/group_gain_effect.png'],'comparison_rule':{'rtol':1e-6,'numeric':'Frozen helper tolerance for numerical outputs','nonnumeric':'Exact output comparison','ignore_as_scientific_difference':['timestamps','logs','prose','formatting'],'stochastic':'No special stochastic tolerance; fixed seed and 5000 permutations documented'},'attempts':[{'command_record':'formal-replay-attempt.json','stdout':'replay-runner.stdout','stderr':'replay-runner.stderr','outcome':'Failed before materialization because the requested workdir already existed; no target code ran.'},{'command_record':'replay-runner-2.stdout','stdout':'replay-runner-2.stdout','stderr':'replay-runner-2.stderr','outcome':'Wrapper rejected invocation because formal replay allowance was consumed; no copy or target execution.'}],'assessor_workflow_limitation':'The first invalid invocation consumed the frozen wrapper allowance, preventing a valid single replay. This does not measure target behavior.','comparison':'Unavailable; no generated replay outputs.'}\n(out/'replay-record.json').write_text(json.dumps(replay,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build_assessment.py\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build-assessment.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build-assessment.stderr\"; status=$?; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build-assessment.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/build-assessment.stderr\"; printf '\"'build_exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
